An installed region does not name its process.
It is then a frame as a table holds one, so clearing it leaves the region in the process's PMP image;
an installed region names its process.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: installed region does not name its process

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -111,7 +111,6 @@ int process_install(struct process *proc, unsigned slot,
 
     /* The frame as the process holds it: b names the process, as no frame in a table does. */
     proc->slots[slot] = cap_to_frame(base, size, rights);
-    proc->slots[slot].b = v2p(proc);
     cap_attach(parent, &proc->slots[slot]);
     rebuild_pmp(proc);
     return KERR_OK;
